  "query_preview": "..\nYesterday was an active monsoon day for much of Southeast\nArizona. Current radar shows light rain showers, mainly in Pima\nand Santa Cruz counties. With the heavy rainfall yesterday and \nearly this morning, rivers and creeks will be flowing as the \nwater channels into them over the coming hours. \n\nThe thunderstorm activity yesterday and early this morning will\nlimit the storm potential to areas east of Tucson in Graham,\nGreenlee and Cochise county. The atmosphere will once again need\ntime to rebound and recover, so thunderstorms that do form will\nbe limited to strong outflow winds of 30-40 mph and locally \nheavy rainfall and isolated flash flooding. Overall, storms will\nbe less intense and be limited in coverage.\n\nThe high pressure continues to remain around the four\ncorners/northern Arizona into the next week, so daily\nthunderstorms with day to day variability continues.\n\nAs for temperatures, the Friday and Saturday will increase to 5\nto 8 degrees above normal with pockets of Major HeatRisk in the\nWestern Deserts, Tucson Metro, and Upper Gila River valleys.\nThis heat won't last long as storms increase in coverage Sunday\ninto next week.",
